Only the dependency closure needed for actual analytic division, analytic
germ rings, Rückert's Noetherian theorem, and a prepared quotient's finite
power basis is retained. The coefficient field is changed from complex to
real. The real preparation proof is independently attributed in
third_party/classical-complex-wpt/NOTICE.

Adapted source areas: WPTBridge/DivisionCore.lean, WPTBridge/Division.lean,
WPTBridge/DivisionUniqueness.lean, Germs/Basic.lean, Germs/Ring.lean,
Germs/Coordinates.lean, WPTBridge/GermDivision.lean,
Algebra/NoetherianByRemainder.lean, WPTBridge/Preparation.lean,
WPTBridge/PreparedAssociate.lean,
Noetherian/Ruckert.lean, and FiniteProjection/PreparedQuotient.lean.

The modules are split into Transformer.AnalyticPreparation and
Transformer.RealAnalyticGerms. Unused hypotheses and unrelated interfaces
are removed. Mathlib 4.34 adaptations include LinearEquiv.ofLinearMap.
New modules add nonlinear analytic pullbacks, finite equation bases, monic
analytic representative relations, exact-degree characteristic-polynomial
relations for fiber values, and concrete joint witnesses.

Complex Nullstellensatz, complex geometric finite projections, surjectivity
of projections, and claims requiring existence of complex roots are not
copied or asserted over the real field. No package dependency is added.
